== About Me

I am currently a Ph.D. student in Computational Mathematics at Shanghai Normal University, working under the supervision of Prof. [https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=ZBKemyIAAAAJ Qian Guo]. 
My research focuses on the intersection of numerical analysis and machine learning, with particular interests in neural networks, numerical methods for stochastic differential equations, and AI for control systems.

Before starting my doctoral studies, I completed my M.S. in Computational Mathematics at Shanghai Normal University under the supervision of Dr. [https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=CvM-APQAAAAJ Wei Liu], where I worked on numerical methods for stochastic differential equations.

I have been awarded funding from the China Scholarship Council (CSC) and will visit the University of Birmingham in the United Kingdom for a one-year CSC-funded research visit under the supervision of Dr. [https://sites.google.com/site/xiaochengshang Xiaocheng Shang].

== News

- *Talk* (November 2026): Safe neural control for a stationary distribution of stochastic functional differential equations. Joint with X. Mao and Q. Guo. 14th Student Forum of the Technical Committee on Control Theory (TCCT). {{<a href="files/slides/TCCT2026.pdf">[slides]</a>}}
- *Preprint* (October 2026): Numerical methods for nonlinear stochastic differential equations driven by subdiffusion. Joint with Q. Guo and W. Liu. \[[https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.41550 arXiv]\]
- *Preprint* (October 2026): Strong convergence of fully discrete tamed Euler approximations for time-changed stochastic delay differential equations. Joint with Q. Guo. \[[https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.28552 arXiv]\]
- *Preprint* (August 2026): A diffusion time-changed stochastic SIS epidemic model: well-posedness, long-time behavior, and numerical approximation. Joint with X. Li and H. Zhou. \[[https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.21930 arXiv]\]
- *Accepted* (August 2026): Stability of equidistant-step Euler-type methods for time-changed stochastic differential equations. Joint with Z. Rong. /Statistics & Probability Letters/. \[[https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0167715226003147 paper]\]
- *Talk* (August 2026): The 4th Graduate Forum on Numerical Methods for Stochastic Differential Equations. {{<a href="files/slides/Tianyuan2026.pdf">[slides]</a>}}
- *Accepted* (July 2026): A Milstein-type method for highly non-linear non-autonomous time-changed stochastic differential equations. Joint with R. Wu. /Applied Numerical Mathematics/. \[[https://doi.org/10.1016/j.apnum.2026.07.013 paper]\]
- *Online* (July 2026): Parameter-related strong convergence rates of Euler-type methods for time-changed stochastic differential equations. /Numerical Algorithms/. \[[https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s11075-026-02454-0 paper]\]

